     This appears to be a case of "You can't get there from here."
The code for the win32 interface supports both ascii_fit_to_screen
and tiles_fit_to_screen, but the core code that parses options only
has "fit_to_screen" and uses it to set up ascii_fit_to_screen.

     There is a comment (in include/winprocs.h) which says that
map_mode is deprecated, but it doesn't mention what the preferred
replacement is.

     You can use the F4 key as a shortcut for interactively toggling
fit-to-screen (for either ascii or tiles, whichever is currently in
use) on or off without resorting to that menu.


